+// ---- USB runtime-PM wake-up recovery (state 0) ----
+//
+// The hwdb marks 27c6:55a4 autosuspend-capable (usb:v27C6p55A4* ->
+// ID_AUTOSUSPEND=1), so the kernel suspends it after a couple of idle seconds.
+// The firmware can resume with the control endpoint alive (~1 ms on EP0) while
+// bulk-OUT stays wedged: every OUT is NAKed until a USB port reset, so the
+// session's first command (the state-0 NOP) dies at GOODIX_TIMEOUT
+// ("transfer timed out") and fprintd reports enroll-unknown-error. Nothing
+// self-heals; the device stays wedged for the rest of the boot.
+//
+// Raw usbfs probes on real hardware: g_usb_device_reset() with the interface
+// still claimed (the same port reset enumeration performs, no NVM/config
+// involvement), then the same NOP again, is accepted immediately, ENABLE_CHIP
+// gets its ACK, and the device survives the next suspend/resume cycle. One
+// deferred retry restores it for good.
